<title>SYRIA: Syria buys 26,000 T white/raw sugar.</title>
<headline>Syria buys 26,000 T white/raw sugar.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's general foreign trade organisation for chemicals and foostuffs (GEZA) bought 26,000 tonnes of white and raw sugar on Thursday for delivery between Feburary 15 and March 17, a Geza official said.</p>
<p>He told Reuters that 13,000 tonnes of white sugar was bought from Japanese company Tomen at $344 and the other cargo of 13,000 tonnes of raws was bought from french trader Lorico at $290.4.</p>
</text>
